{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And you shall take of the first.</b> It went back over it in order to teach you the order of the commandments." "<b>Of the first.</b> Rashi explained: and not all of the first. That is, you are not required to bring all of the fruit in its entirety, but part of it. Another interpretation: <b>of the first</b> — of the choicest, as in ״ראשית תבואתו״, ״ראשית שמנים ימשחו״, which is an expression of praise and choiceness. Another interpretation: <b>of the first</b> — from those that ripen first, because they are the most cherished." "<b>All the fruit of the land.</b> You bring fruit as first fruits, but you do not bring wine and oil for first fruits." "<b>And you shall place in a basket.</b> In a manner of honor — and not in the lap and not in the fold of the garment." "<b>And you shall go to the place.</b> The owner of the first fruits himself must do everything — the gathering and the going — and not by means of an agent. And so is the custom: if the king gave a field to his servant, the servant himself brings him a gift from the fruits of the field."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:18.493076102Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}